"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, ftl.apworld or ftl_mv.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. Then, preloaded ftlman content will then be installed into the game's core folder. The AP Mod's file and the Multiverse mod Assets and Data folders will be installed inside the 'ftlman\\mods' directory. At the end of the setup, the mod manager will open, simply make sure that on the left, all the mods are selected (highlighted in blue). Now select 1.23.1 on the Hyperspace option. Then hit 'Scan' and finally 'Apply' and you can start playing.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"FTL is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'ftl.apworld' or 'ftl_mv.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up you should see a new Archipelago connection window at the bottom-left corner of the main menu.\n\nIn the 'Address' field, enter 'archipelago.gg'.\n\nIn the 'Port' field, enter the port. This is a 5-digit number that you can find on the website after creating a new room.\n\nIn 'Slot name', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nFinally, click 'Connect' and then, you can start a new run on a new save!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for FTL Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear' option it will delete everything related to ftlman, Hyperspace, mods, restore the original files that were replaced and verify the game files integrity. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.",
